# clang-tidy configuration for loftail (CLAUDE.md, "Stack" and "Commands").
#
# Two routes read this one file:
#   * -DLOFTAIL_CLANG_TIDY=ON, which puts clang-tidy on the compile line of the
#     three src/ targets;
#   * the standalone `clang_tidy` / `clang_tidy_all` targets, which drive
#     run-clang-tidy over compile_commands.json.
# Keeping the config in one place is what stops the two disagreeing.
#
# Nothing here is WarningsAsErrors. The tree has never been linted, so there is a
# standing baseline; a build that refuses to finish on it is a build people work
# around. The CI job is non-blocking for the same reason.
#
# NOT enabled, deliberately:
#   cppcoreguidelines-*            almost every check in it fires on ordinary Qt
#                                  code (pro-type-vararg on qDebug, pro-bounds-*
#                                  on every array, owning-memory on `new QWidget`).
#                                  Worth revisiting once the baseline is at zero.
#   readability-identifier-naming  the tree is already consistently Qt-styled and a
#                                  naming table is a large surface to get wrong.

Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cert-err58-cpp,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding,
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  -modernize-use-nodiscard,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-else-after-return,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-magic-numbers

# Why each exclusion, in the order it appears above. The counts are from the first
# full sweep over src/ with clang-tidy 21: 3918 reported lines (997 distinct
# findings; a header is re-reported once per TU that includes it) before these came
# off, 805 lines / 408 distinct after. A count is quoted where the count IS the
# argument; where the check is simply wrong for this tree the count is beside the
# point.
#
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#       Qt APIs and the geometry helpers take runs of same-typed ints by design
#       (x, y, w, h; first, last; before, after). Every one of them is a finding.
#   cert-err58-cpp
#       fires on every file-scope QString/QRegularExpression constant, which is how
#       the parse and format tables are written.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding                             12 findings
#       ELEVEN of the twelve are the same one: Document.h, re-reported once per TU
#       that includes it. It is an opt-in layout hint, and invariant #1 is about
#       Record — 32 bytes, one per indexed line — not about the one Document per
#       open log. The rest of clang-analyzer-* stays on; this is the only check in
#       it that is switched off.
#   misc-const-correctness                                              208 findings
#       proposes `const QApplication app` in main.cpp and const-qualified locals
#       that are then moved from. The genuinely useful subset is not worth 208.
#   misc-include-cleaner
#       wants a direct #include for every symbol, against Qt's umbrella headers.
#   misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes
#       Record (invariant #1, exactly 32 bytes), FormatSettings, LogProfile,
#       MatchCriteria and the rest of the settings structs are aggregates on purpose.
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#       the static tables (kPriorityByIndex, the palette bands) are C arrays for a
#       reason: constant-initialised, no allocation, usable in a constexpr context.
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers
#       C++20, and noisy against every Qt struct.
#   modernize-use-nodiscard                                            2018 findings
#       51% of the entire baseline on its own: an annotation on every const accessor
#       in 96 headers. Qt does not mark its own getters [[nodiscard]], so adopting it
#       would make loftail's headers read unlike the framework they sit on — the
#       exact thing CLAUDE.md Conventions asks not to happen.
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type
#       would rewrite every signature in the tree, for the same reason.
#   performance-enum-size                                               228 findings
#       every one says "use std::uint8_t". These enums are classifications passed in
#       registers, not fields of the 32-byte Record; and Priority in particular is
#       declared in severity order so a minimum-level filter is one >= (invariant #4),
#       which narrowing its base type buys nothing for.
#   portability-avoid-pragma-once                                       647 findings
#       one per header, because every header in the tree opens with #pragma once.
#       That is the project's convention and all four supported toolchains honour it.
#   readability-braces-around-statements, readability-else-after-return
#       pure style, and there is no .clang-format enforcing a matching shape.
#   readability-function-cognitive-complexity
#       one unactionable finding each for MainWindow.cpp and LogView.cpp.
#   readability-identifier-length
#       r, dx, ok are the local idiom.
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion
#       `if (ptr)` on a Qt pointer is universal here.
#   readability-magic-numbers
#       the geometry code is measured pixel and character constants, which is the
#       point of it (ARCHITECTURE.md §7.1.1); every one is deliberate and commented.
#
# Kept ON deliberately, against its count: bugprone-narrowing-conversions, 292
# findings, 144 of them in RecordIndex.h and 48 in FilteredIndex.h. That is not an
# accident of where the qsizetype/int mixing happens to be — it is precisely the
# two-level prefix-sum geometry where the documented scroll-range overflow lives
# ("the scroll range is qBound-ed into int, not cast", ARCHITECTURE.md §7.1.1). A
# check whose findings cluster on the code that has already been bitten by that
# class stays on.

# THE TWO CLANG-TIDY VERSIONS DISAGREE, ON PURPOSE. CI pins 18 (what Ubuntu 24.04
# ships, ARCHITECTURE.md §1) and a dev machine has whatever it has — 21 here, which
# is what the counts above were measured with. Checks that arrived after 18 are
# simply absent there: portability-avoid-pragma-once is one of the exclusions above
# and matches nothing under 18, while readability-use-concise-preprocessor-directives
# (41 findings here) and modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison (34) are enabled and
# report nothing there. An unknown name in the list is inert, never an error, so
# neither half needs guarding. Do NOT delete a name because the local binary does
# not know it — check which version ADDED it first.

# Only loftail's own headers. Qt's are not ours to fix, and the dev machine's Qt
# (6.10) is newer than the reference build's (6.4) — a diagnostic from a Qt header
# would differ between this box and CI for reasons that have nothing to do with us.
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(src/(core|ui|bench)|tests)/[^/]*\.h$'

WarningsAsErrors: ''
FormatStyle: none
